        "title": "feat(durable): add beta3 runtime core foundation",
        "body": "# PR2/5 — runtime foundation/core + terminal immutability guard\n\n## Context capsule\n\nThis PR is item 2 of the rebuilt beta3 durable core stack. It asks reviewers to evaluate the runtime foundation/core + terminal immutability guard slice on its own base while recognizing that later PRs build cumulatively on top.\n\n## Durable core stack overview\n\n- PR1/5 — docs/RFC/boundary anchor and proof plan.\n- PR2/5 — runtime foundation/core plus terminal SQLite row immutability guard.\n- PR3/5 — wake targets, durable producers, replay/resume semantics.\n- PR4/5 — controls/inspection plus CLI/Gateway surface.\n- PR5/5 — internal session delivery handoff, final hardening, and cumulative E proof.\n\n## Stack position\n\n- Stack item: PR2/5\n- Current PR summary: Durable store/runtime foundation, session/task primitives, gateway/CLI protocol foundation, terminal SQLite row immutability guard.\n- Does not claim: No wake-target/replay controls/internal handoff; no plugin SDK DTS size fix.\n- Dependency/base: `5d9fb965cada2083c532c68cc9b95fb0f4f7d7a2` (PR1 public submitted head, https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/104246)\n- Downstream dependency: PR3 depends on this PR\n- Canonical upstream gate(s): PR1 has ClawSweeper threshold met (`platinum hermit`) and awaits maintainer decision; PR2 was rebased and verified after syncing PR1 private branch.\n- This PR head: `codex/openclaw-durable-beta3-newstack-pr2-runtime-core` at `2e4129630ac2e90fe6fe66236d8e1309795d3827`\n- Intended base: `5d9fb965cada2083c532c68cc9b95fb0f4f7d7a2`\n\n## Dependency / promotion gate\n\n- Submit/merge gate: PR2 should only be promoted after its base is canonical and threshold-met.\n- Current gate state: PR1 reviewer threshold met; PR2 exact-head ancestry and local proof pass after rebase.\n- Next dependent PR: PR3 depends on this PR.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nDurable store/runtime foundation, session/task primitives, gateway/CLI protocol foundation, terminal SQLite row immutability guard. This narrows review to the intended durable-runtime layer, keeps the cumulative stack ancestry clean, and gives reviewers exact-head evidence instead of relying on stale or downstream proof.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Durable store/runtime foundation, session/task primitives, gateway/CLI protocol foundation, terminal SQLite row immutability guard.\n- Exact-head local status captured in `new-pr2-build-status.md` and refreshed by the PR2 promotion status artifact.\n- Branch/head/base captured in `new-5pr-stack-final-audit.md`.\n\n## Non-scope\n\n- No wake-target/replay controls/internal handoff; no plugin SDK DTS size fix.\n- No wake-target/replay controls/internal handoff is part of this slice.\n- No plugin SDK DTS size fix is included in the durable behavior narrative.\n\n## Base / diff hygiene\n\n- Base comparison: `5d9fb965cada2083c532c68cc9b95fb0f4f7d7a2..2e4129630ac2e90fe6fe66236d8e1309795d3827`\n- Non-cumulative check: `git merge-base --is-ancestor 5d9fb965cada2083c532c68cc9b95fb0f4f7d7a2 codex/openclaw-durable-beta3-newstack-pr2-runtime-core` passed after PR2 rebase.\n- Conflict/replay notes: PR2 rebased cleanly from old PR1 head `8681317a9ec25fd14bf2253eb77c4d8abba3a41a` onto current PR1 head `5d9fb965cada2083c532c68cc9b95fb0f4f7d7a2`; intentional scope exclusions documented in status artifacts.\n\n## Proof matrix\n\n| Gate | Command / artifact | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Unit / focused behavior | exact-head rerun after rebase | passed locally on `2e4129630ac2e90fe6fe66236d8e1309795d3827` |\n| Typecheck / static | `pnpm tsgo:core` and docs map check | passed |\n| Diff hygiene | `git diff --check 5d9fb965cada2083c532c68cc9b95fb0f4f7d7a2..HEAD` and ancestry check | passed |\n| Upgrade/schema, if applicable | status artifact and generated schema diffs | applicable for runtime/schema PRs; docs-only for PR1 |\n| Live proof, if applicable | status artifact | not run in final audit; add before promotion if required |\n\n## Live proof\n\n- Environment: local worktree only for this promotion pass.\n- Result: Remote/Testbox proof was not rerun; existing status artifact records earlier crabbox sanity blocker. Local exact-head focused proof passed after rebase. Runtime live proof should be added before final merge if required.\n- Artifact(s): `new-pr2-build-status.md`, `new-5pr-stack-final-audit.md`, PR2 promotion status artifact.\n\n## ClawSweeper requirements\n\n- Includes authored `What Problem This Solves` section: yes.\n- Includes authored `Evidence`/proof content: yes.\n- Names stored data model / migration impact when schema or persisted state changes: yes; durable state/schema impact is covered in status artifact.\n- Names risk labels ClawSweeper should evaluate: compatibility, session-state, message-delivery, durable-runtime, diff-hygiene.\n- Keeps proof artifacts accessible in body or durable stack state.\n\n## Risk / upgrade notes\n\n- Runtime risk: durable runtime/session behavior changes require exact-head and live proof before promotion.\n- Compatibility/upgrade risk: schema/runtime compatibility must be reviewed against generated state schema and status artifact evidence.\n- Rollback/feature-flag posture: stack is cumulative; rollback should revert/promote by PR boundary rather than cherry-picking descendants.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused durable/unit/commands/gateway/protocol/agents tests passed locally after rebase:\n  - durable unit: 16 files, 68 tests\n  - durable command: 1 file, 7 tests\n  - gateway bundle: 12 files, 863 tests\n  - gateway protocol: 1 file, 51 tests\n  - agent/session adjacent shards: 11 files, 431 tests\n- `pnpm tsgo:core` and `pnpm docs:map:gen --check` passed.\n- `git diff --check 5d9fb965cada2083c532c68cc9b95fb0f4f7d7a2..HEAD` passed.\n- Scope exclusion grep found no `src/durable/wake-*`, `src/durable/wake-controls-inspection*`, `src/durable/wake-internal-delivery*`, or `scripts/write-plugin-sdk-entry-dts.ts` paths.\n- Final ancestry audit passed for `5d9fb965cada2083c532c68cc9b95fb0f4f7d7a2` -> `codex/openclaw-durable-beta3-newstack-pr2-runtime-core` at `2e4129630ac2e90fe6fe66236d8e1309795d3827`.\n\n## Next gate\n\nReview this PR after PR1; PR3 remains private until PR2 reaches the configured reviewer threshold.\n",
